## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates knowledge of edge ML deployment, covering model optimization, over-the-air updates, and monitoring strategies for resource-constrained environments.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference using SageMaker Edge Manager
- Model quantization (INT8) for ARM64 architecture
- OTA updates via AWS IoT Jobs with rollback slots
- Local telemetry and validation with intermittent connectivity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Model inference with latency tracking
const model = loadModel('arm_int8.tflite');
const t0 = performance.now();
const output = model.run(input);
const latency = performance.now() - t0;

// Emit telemetry for edge agent
emitTelemetry({ latency, outputQuality: evaluateQuality(output) });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design secure, scalable multi-tenant inference with cross-account PrivateLink, model registry usage, and drift-aware rollouts under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines
- PrivateLink across AWS accounts
- Multi-tenant isolation strategies (shared vs. per-tenant containers)
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(input, modelRegistry) {
  const tenant = input.tenantId;
  if (!allowedTenants.has(tenant)) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized tenant');
  }
  const modelVersion = modelRegistry.getModelVersion(tenant, 'latest');
  return invokeSageMaker(modelVersion.endpoint, input);
}
```

